1
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:18,120
Two weeks. I said I could do it in two weeks, and I did it.

2
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:21,360
The pictures you've taken are fabulous, Richard.

3
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,170
Mr. Carlson will love them.

4
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:25,060
Monday morning.

5
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:27,200
I'm going to show him the photos on Monday morning.

6
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:31,040
I can't wait!

7
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:37,070
I'm very proud of you. You really did a beautiful job.

8
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:41,770
I know he will love the new photographs for your book.

9
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:46,750
Yeah. I really did do a good job, didn't I?

10
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:50,490
Hey, you know? There's still some film left on this roll,

11
00:02:50,490 --> 00:02:52,990
and there's one person I haven't photographed in a long time.

12
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:53,750
Who?

13
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,690
You.

14
00:02:55,690 --> 00:02:59,100
Richard! I haven't brushed my hair. Richard,

15
00:02:59,100 --> 00:02:59,720
You look great!

16
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:06,970
It's not fair, Richard. I'm not even ready.

17
00:03:06,970 --> 00:03:34,310
Oh, that's wonderful! That's wonderful!

18
00:03:34,310 --> 00:03:37,740
Thanks.

19
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:38,520
Fabulous!

20
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,990
Thanks.

21
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:43,050
Terrific!

22
00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:44,490
Thanks.

23
00:03:44,490 --> 00:03:46,990
They get better and better.

24
00:03:46,990 --> 00:03:50,400
Thanks a lot.

25
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,770
This is sensational!

26
00:03:51,770 --> 00:03:55,320
Yeah. Thanks.

27
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,830
What a job! Good work, Richard!

28
00:03:58,830 --> 00:04:01,260
I'm so glad you like them so much.

29
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:05,110
Like them? They represent your best work.

30
00:04:05,110 --> 00:04:06,020
Really?

31
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:08,120
Absolutely.

32
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:14,380
Well ... what do you think? Do I have my book?

33
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:22,030
You do. You do. There's a book here.

34
00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:23,400
I'll have a contract

35
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,660
and an advance payment waiting for you

36
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,740
first thing in the morning.

37
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:27,900
Thank you.

38
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,250
And while you're here,

39
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:30,460
I would like to introduce you to your editor.

40
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:34,220
And I want you to meet the people in the art department.

41
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:36,150
I'll set up an appointment with the marketing people.

42
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:38,510
When do you think we'll be through?

43
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:41,530
In about half an hour. Why?

44
00:04:41,530 --> 00:04:44,530
I can't wait to tell Marilyn!
